&lt;li&gt;Own and mature CoreWeave’s product regulatory governance program, including product-review processes, approval frameworks, policies, decision records, training, control mappings, and evidence demonstrating compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead legal review of new and evolving products, features, AI capabilities, data uses, and infrastructure initiatives throughout the product lifecycle; identify requirements, conduct international product regulatory risk assessments, and recommend controls, approvals, and launch conditions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product and Engineering to embed privacy by design and default, responsible AI, security, data-governance, transparency, and other requirements into product architecture, roadmaps, and development processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise Supply Chain and Global Operations on product-related regulatory matters, including technology transitions, state packaging requirements, equipment compliance, and scalable supply-chain regulatory programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product Commercial Legal to align product functionality, customer commitments, contracting positions, disclosures, technical documentation, and marketing claims with legal requirements and approved controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor, interpret, and operationalize U.S. and international product, privacy, AI, data, cybersecurity, consumer-protection, and digital-services laws; advise senior leadership on product roadmaps, market entry, and business models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead significant regulatory inquiries, audits, investigations, and policy engagements involving CoreWeave’s products and services; coordinate cross-functional responses, oversee outside counsel, drive remediation, and provide subject-matter leadership across Legal and Compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of relevant legal experience, including substantial experience counseling complex technology products; a mix of law firm and in-house experience is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to serve as the senior legal advisor to Product and Engineering leaders and independently resolve novel, high-impact regulatory issues throughout the product lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in multiple regulatory areas relevant to AI and cloud products, such as AI governance, privacy and data protection, cybersecurity, consumer protection, data regulation, or digital-services regulation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical fluency and the ability to translate product functionality, system architecture, data flows, model behavior, and technical documentation into clear legal and engineering actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing and leading product governance programs, including review and approval frameworks, policies, controls, training, audit-ready evidence, and monitoring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience conducting international product risk assessments and advising on market entry, product launches, technology transitions, and cross-border requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional judgment and executive presence, with the ability to identify material risk, present practical options, and make defensible recommendations in ambiguous situations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent drafting and communication skills, including the ability to influence senior technical and business leaders and explain complex regulatory requirements clearly and concisely.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead through influence, build trusted cross-functional relationships, coordinate complex initiatives across multiple teams, and provide subject-matter leadership without direct management authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;J.D. from an accredited law school and active membership in at least one U.S. state bar (NY, NJ, CA, DC, or WA preferred).&lt;/li&gt;
