&lt;p&gt;As &lt;strong&gt;Counsel, Commercial,&lt;/strong&gt; you will support our rapidly growing Global Field Organization (GFO) business. If you thrive in a dynamic, fast-paced environment, enjoy solving complex problems, and are eager to make a significant impact, CoreWeave is the place for you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Director and Managing Assistant General Counsel - Commercial Americas, you will partner closely with Sales, Product, Security, Privacy, Finance, and Operations teams to support complex commercial cloud sales, SaaS, and Infrastructure/IaaS transactions with enterprise customers and strategic partners. You will play a key role in negotiating agreements, advising on legal and commercial risk, and helping scale the legal processes that support CoreWeave’s continued growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this role, you will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft, review, and negotiate complex commercial technology agreements with enterprise customers, including cloud services, SaaS, infrastructure/IaaS, software licensing, professional services, partnership, and data processing agreements.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with CoreWeave’s Global Field Organization (GFO) teams to support enterprise sales cycles and drive customer transactions to successful outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise internal stakeholders on legal, privacy, and commercial risks arising from customer transactions and recommend practical solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage multiple concurrent transactions while balancing legal risk, business objectives, and operational efficiency for a fast-moving sales organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support strategic customer engagements by providing practical, business-oriented legal guidance throughout the transaction lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and escalate novel, complex, or high-risk issues while exercising sound legal and business judgment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help develop and improve contract templates, playbooks, policies, and processes that enable efficient and scalable support for a rapidly growing global business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with outside counsel when needed to support specialized legal matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;JD degree and active membership in at least one U.S. state bar.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of combined legal experience in-house and/or at a law firm, with primary focus on commercial technology transactions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting fast paced enterprise sales organizations and negotiating complex customer agreements, including SaaS, IaaS, cloud services, software licensing, and other technology offerings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience negotiating data processing agreements and identifying privacy and data protection issues in commercial transactions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to independently manage complex commercial contract negotiations while exercising sound judgment regarding escalation and risk tolerance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to provide practical business-oriented legal advice in a fast-paced environment.Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to effectively influence stakeholders and build trusted cross-functional relationships across the organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional attention to detail and organizational skills, with the ability to manage multiple competing priorities and drive matters to resolution efficiently and effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Growth-oriented mindset, with a demonstrated ability to incorporate feedback, continuously develop expertise, and adapt to evolving business needs and responsibilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
