&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Legal and Government Affairs (LGA)&amp;nbsp; team at CoreWeave is highly collaborative and partners closely with teams across the company to navigate complex legal landscapes while enabling innovation and growth. The team is pragmatic, solutions-oriented, and deeply engaged in strategic decision-making, with a strong emphasis on building trusted relationships across the organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As &lt;strong&gt;Counsel, Global Supply Chain,&lt;/strong&gt; you will play a critical role in helping CoreWeave secure and deploy the infrastructure that powers our business. Working alongside Supply Chain and Capacity Operations, you will provide strategic legal support across the sourcing, procurement, and deployment of GPUs, servers, networking equipment, storage solutions, data center infrastructure, and global logistics. You&#39;ll help structure complex commercial relationships, develop scalable contracting processes, and advise the business on legal and regulatory issues that directly impact CoreWeave&#39;s global growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the&lt;strong&gt; Director &amp;amp; Managing Associate General Counsel, Global Supply Chain&lt;/strong&gt;, you will serve as a senior individual contributor on the Legal &amp;amp; Government Affairs team embedded with our Supply Chain and Capacity Operations organization.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support &lt;strong&gt;datacenter supply chain&lt;/strong&gt;, including by structuring, drafting, and negotiating complex agreements with suppliers for the procurement of GPU and compute hardware, integrated server systems, network equipment, datacenter infrastructure and power equipment, storage solutions, and logistics services. Collaborate closely with cross-functional partners across finance, tax, compliance, energy, real estate on deal structuring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support &lt;strong&gt;indirect procurement &lt;/strong&gt;contracting for business groups across the company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide &lt;strong&gt;day-to-day, business-focused counseling&lt;/strong&gt;, including on supply chain continuity, risk allocation, supplier risk assessments, supplier performance and remediation matters, product quality, service, and remedies aligned with CoreWeave’s deployment and financing models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with regulatory, ESG, government affairs, compliance, and others on &lt;strong&gt;responsible sourcing and compliance&lt;/strong&gt; topics and ensure contract terms reflect those obligations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support &lt;strong&gt;international expansion&lt;/strong&gt; by adapting supply and logistics documentation for new jurisdictions and coordinating with local counsel on local-law and market-norm issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage &lt;strong&gt;outside counsel&lt;/strong&gt; on specialized matters and convert advice into clear, usable guidance for business stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop,maintain and scale &lt;strong&gt;templates, playbooks, and fallbacks&lt;/strong&gt; that drive consistent, efficient negotiations and scalable self-service for sourcing and logistics teams. Contribute to &lt;strong&gt;training and enablement&lt;/strong&gt; so business teams can handle common scenarios with less friction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Juris Doctor (JD) from an accredited law school; active bar membership in at least one U.S. jurisdiction (or international equivalent).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of legal experience, including significant time focused on complex commercial transactions at a law firm or in-house legal team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong business acumen and meaningful experience drafting and negotiating technology infrastructure, hardware, or supply-chain agreements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven record of pragmatic, solutions-oriented counseling for senior business leaders in a demanding, high-growth, fast-paced environment, with sound judgment on balancing risk with agility to deliver outcomes with aggressive timelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-house experience supporting cloud, data center, semiconductor, hardware, or similar large-scale infrastructure businesses.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to global logistics and trade controls, sanctions, and hardware environmental compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or operating contracting playbooks, templates, and processes for sourcing or procurement organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of international trade, hardware regulatory requirements, and other compliance issues and structures pertaining to global supply chains.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wondering if you’re a good fit? &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We believe in investing in our people, and value candidates who can bring their own diversified experiences to our teams – even if you aren&#39;t a 100% skill or experience match.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; Here are a few qualities we’ve found compatible with our team. If some of this describes you, we’d love to talk.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical, solution-oriented and ready to roll up your sleeves.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills and a demonstrated ability to work collaboratively in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re curious about how AI, cloud, and digital infrastructure are reshaping the global economy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why CoreWeave?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At CoreWeave, we work hard, have fun, and move fast!&amp;nbsp; We’re in an exciting stage of hyper-growth that you will not want to miss out on. We’re not afraid of a little chaos, and we’re constantly learning. Our team cares deeply about how we build our product and how we work together, which is represented through our core values:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be Curious at Your Core&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act Like an Owner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Empower Employees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver Best-in-Class Client Experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Achieve More Together&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We support and encourage an entrepreneurial outlook and independent thinking. We foster an environment that encourages collaboration and enables the development of innovative solutions to complex problems. As we get set for takeoff, the organization&#39;s growth opportunities are constantly expanding. You will be surrounded by some of the best talent in the industry, who will want to learn from you, too. Come join us!&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base salary range for this role is $134,000 to $179,000. The starting salary will be determined by job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and the market location. We strive for both market alignment and internal equity when determining compensation. In addition to base salary, our total rewards package includes a discretionary bonus, equity awards, and a comprehensive benefits program (all based on eligibility).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The range we’ve posted represents the typical compensation range for this role. To determine actual compensation, we review the market rate for each candidate which can include a variety of factors. These include qualifications, experience, interview performance, and location.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to a competitive salary, we offer a variety of benefits to support your needs. The benefits below reflect our US-based offerings for full-time employees; for roles in other locations, benefits vary and are shared during the hiring process. These include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medical, dental, and vision insurance - 100% paid for by CoreWeave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company-paid Life Insurance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Voluntary supplemental life insurance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Short and long-term disability insurance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible Spending Account&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health Savings Account&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tuition Reimbursement&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to Participate in Employee Stock Purchase Program (ESPP)&lt;/li&gt;
