&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an SME for Data Center Commission and Quality. This role demands direct knowledge of data center construction, with a strong focus on MEP systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working directly with CoreWeave project coordination members, you will ensure projects across the CoreWeave portfolio are completed on time and to the highest quality standards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Responsibilities include overseeing the installation and testing of components and systems, including mission-critical systems such as generators, UPS systems, electrical distribution equipment, redundancy protocols, and cooling systems such as chillers and CDUs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a remote-eligible position with 50% travel required. Candidates must reside in or near the Northern Virginia, Dallas, Richmond, Virginia, Livingston, New Jersey, or Atlanta, Georgia regions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate with safety at the forefront of all construction initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;As necessary, collaborate with general contractors, trade partners, and vendors.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a liaison between clients and internal teams, facilitating communication during commissioning activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review all written documentation, commissioning, and quality-related information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in developing, reviewing, and implementing commissioning plans as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in coordinating and attending pre-construction commissioning meetings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attend construction progress and pre-installation job-site meetings to gather relevant information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review meeting minutes for necessary revisions and assist in resolving design-intent discrepancies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inspect field installations and witness functional tests; conduct site visits as necessary.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Witness the execution of commissioning tests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel to sites, client meetings, and training as required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in developing reports that define project progress, problems, and solutions for leadership teams and clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in MEP (Mechanical, Electrical, and Plumbing) commissioning, with a preference for experience in data centers or critical facility environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive understanding of data center infrastructure, including Building Management Systems (BMS), Electrical Power Monitoring Systems (EPMS), and complex MEP building systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with local building codes and industry-standard frameworks, including &lt;strong&gt;NEC, NFPA, IEEE, and ASHRAE&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite (Excel, Word, Outlook) and experience with industry-standard commissioning software or digital platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously, maintaining high organizational standards and meeting strict project deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-directed professional with a proven track record of driving complex processes to completion and ensuring accountability across the project lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to develop and maintain effective professional relationships with contractors, clients, and cross-functional internal teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience in the coordination, commissioning, or quality assurance of electrical and low-voltage equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Possession of a valid driver’s license and a motor vehicle record that meets company insurability standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel up to 50% of the time and the ability to respond to emergency communications outside of standard business hours as required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States at the time of employment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
