&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;3:1-3:20;20-39&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;5:1-5:179;41-219&quot;&gt;CoreWeave is a dynamic, high-growth technology company. We are seeking a Demand Planner to ensure seamless alignment between customer needs and our cloud infrastructure capacity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;7:1-7:20;221-240&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;9:1-9:509;242-750&quot;&gt;In this role, you will work closely with Sales, Solutions Architects, and Engineering teams to manage the customer pipeline, anticipate demand, and proactively address infrastructure availability challenges. Your ability to solve problems and collaborate across teams will help ensure customers receive the right resources at the right time, driving satisfaction and long-term success. By balancing supply and demand effectively, you will play a key role in delivering a smooth and scalable cloud experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;[li_&amp;amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3 print:block print:space-y-1&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;11:1-21:124;752-2084&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;11:1-11:159;752-910&quot;&gt;Develop and maintain demand forecasts for cloud infrastructure resources, factoring in customer pipeline data, market trends, and historical usage patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;12:1-12:116;911-1026&quot;&gt;Align capacity planning with sales projections to ensure the right infrastructure is available at the right time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;13:1-13:124;1027-1150&quot;&gt;Work with engineering and operations teams to optimize supply/demand matching for compute, storage, and network capacity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;14:1-14:156;1151-1306&quot;&gt;Partner with GTM, Solutions Architects, and Product teams to track customer demand signals, translating them into actionable infrastructure requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;15:1-15:106;1307-1412&quot;&gt;Evaluate enterprise customer projects to anticipate capacity needs and minimize deployment bottlenecks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;16:1-16:101;1413-1513&quot;&gt;Identify gaps in supply planning and recommend proactive solutions to support high-priority deals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;17:1-17:141;1514-1654&quot;&gt;Collaborate with Finance, Engineering, and Datacenter Operations teams to optimize resource investments while maintaining cost efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;18:1-18:94;1655-1748&quot;&gt;Provide strategic insights to Leadership on demand trends, capacity constraints, and risks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;19:1-19:125;1749-1873&quot;&gt;Track forecast accuracy, infrastructure utilization rates, and demand variances, making data-driven adjustments as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;20:1-20:87;1874-1960&quot;&gt;Identify process inefficiencies and drive improvements in demand planning workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;21:1-21:124;1961-2084&quot;&gt;Analyze historical demand forecasts and actuals to create dashboards &amp;amp; reporting of key metrics across all product lines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;23:1-23:17;2086-2102&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;[li_&amp;amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3 print:block print:space-y-1&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;25:1-31:62;2104-2818&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;25:1-25:164;2104-2267&quot;&gt;Minimum 3-7 years of experience in demand planning, supply chain management, or capacity planning—ideally in cloud, data center, or IT infrastructure industries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;26:1-26:114;2268-2381&quot;&gt;Excellent communication and collaboration skills to influence stakeholders across technical and business teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;27:1-27:130;2382-2511&quot;&gt;Strong analytical skills with experience in forecasting models and data visualization tools (Excel, SQL, Power BI, or similar).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;28:1-28:63;2512-2574&quot;&gt;Ability to make recommendations in an ambiguous environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;29:1-29:80;2575-2654&quot;&gt;Experience working with demand planning and supply chain management software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;30:1-30:102;2655-2756&quot;&gt;Familiarity with cloud infrastructure components (compute, storage, networking) and how they scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;31:1-31:62;2757-2818&quot;&gt;Ability to thrive in a fast-paced, high-growth environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;33:1-33:36;2820-2855&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wondering if you&#39;re a good fit?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;35:1-35:289;2857-3145&quot;&gt;We believe in investing in our people, and value candidates who can bring their own diversified experiences to our teams – even if you aren&#39;t a 100% skill or experience match.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;41:1-41:19;3213-3231&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why CoreWeave?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;43:1-43:327;3233-3559&quot;&gt;At CoreWeave, we work hard, have fun, and move fast! We&#39;re in an exciting stage of hyper-growth that you will not want to miss out on. We&#39;re not afraid of a little chaos, and we&#39;re constantly learning. Our team cares deeply about how we build our product and how we work together, which is represented through our core values:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;[li_&amp;amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3 print:block print:space-y-1&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;45:1-49:24;3561-3693&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;45:1-45:26;3561-3586&quot;&gt;Be Curious at Your Core&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;46:1-46:20;3587-3606&quot;&gt;Act Like an Owner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;47:1-47:20;3607-3626&quot;&gt;Empower Employees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;48:1-48:43;3627-3669&quot;&gt;Deliver Best-in-Class Client Experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;49:1-49:24;3670-3693&quot;&gt;Achieve More Together&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot; data-sourcepos=&quot;51:1-51:418;3695-4112&quot;&gt;We support and encourage an entrepreneurial outlook and independent thinking. We foster an environment that encourages collaboration and enables the development of innovative solutions to complex problems. As we get set for takeoff, the organization&#39;s growth opportunities are constantly expanding. You will be surrounded by some of the best talent in the industry, who will want to learn from you, too. Come join us!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;The base salary range for this role is $134,000 to $179,000. The starting salary will be determined based on job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and market location. We strive for both market alignment and internal equity when determining compensation. In addition to base salary, our total rewards package includes a discretionary bonus, equity awards, and a comprehensive benefits program (all based on eligibility).&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The range we’ve posted represents the typical compensation range for this role. To determine actual compensation, we review the market rate for each candidate which can include a variety of factors. These include qualifications, experience, interview performance, and location.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to a competitive salary, we offer a variety of benefits to support your needs. The benefits below reflect our US-based offerings for full-time employees; for roles in other locations, benefits vary and are shared during the hiring process. These include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medical, dental, and vision insurance - 100% paid for by CoreWeave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company-paid Life Insurance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Voluntary supplemental life insurance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Short and long-term disability insurance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible Spending Account&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health Savings Account&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tuition Reimbursement&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to Participate in Employee Stock Purchase Program (ESPP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental Wellness Benefits through Spring Health&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family-Forming support provided by Carrot&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid Parental Leave&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible, full-service childcare support with Kinside&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) with a generous employer match&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible PTO&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Catered lunch each day in our office and data center locations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A casual work environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A work culture focused on innovative disruption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;California Applicants&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gPBRBhUNAMBmj7Yn4_M-hCugm7ZJD4hr/view?usp=sharing&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;California Consumer Privacy Act&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity &amp;amp; Accommodations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;CoreWeave is an equal opportunity employer, committed to fostering an inclusive and supportive workplace. All qualified applicants and candidates will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;As part of this commitment and consistent with the &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.eeoc.gov/laws/guidance/fact-sheet-disability-discrimination&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;, CoreWeave will ensure that qualified applicants and candidates with disabilities are provided reasonable accommodations for the hiring process, unless such accommodation would cause an undue hardship. If reasonable accommodation is needed, please contact: &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:careers@coreweave.com&quot;&gt;careers@coreweave.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Export Control Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position requires access to export controlled information. To conform to U.S. Government export regulations applicable to that information, applicant must either be (A) a U.S. person, defined as a (i) U.S. citizen or national, (ii) U.S. lawful permanent resident (green card holder), (iii) refugee under 8 U.S.C. § 1157, or (iv) asylee under 8 U.S.C. § 1158, (B) eligible to access the export controlled information without a required export authorization, or (C) eligible and reasonably likely to obtain the required export authorization from the applicable U.S. government agency. &amp;nbsp;CoreWeave may, for legitimate business reasons, decline to pursue any export licensing process.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;gmail_quote&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;m_1770241969069985273m_-2746164444908759431gmail-docs-internal-guid-131e4fb0-7fff-b4e9-ff50-e8cf32449b1b&quot;&gt;CoreWeave is The Essential Cloud for AI™. Built for pioneers by pioneers, CoreWeave delivers a platform of technology, tools, and teams that enables innovators to build and scale AI with confidence. Trusted by leading AI labs, startups, and global enterprises, CoreWeave combines superior infrastructure performance with deep technical expertise to accelerate breakthroughs and turn compute into capability. Founded in 2017, CoreWeave became a publicly traded company (Nasdaq: CRWV) in March 2025. Learn more at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.coreweave.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-saferedirecturl=&quot;https://www.google.com/url?q=http://www.coreweave.com&amp;amp;source=gmail&amp;amp;ust=1762613132717000&amp;amp;usg=AOvVaw3D-UOhNaqEvF5BEWxjYyAU&quot;&gt;www.coreweave.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Solutions Architecture team at Weights &amp;amp; Biases is a unique hybrid organization, combining the deep technical skills of Site Reliability Engineering with the consultative expertise of Solutions Architecture. We focus on ensuring customers can successfully deploy and operate W&amp;amp;B across cloud and on-prem environments while delivering a best-in-class experience that accelerates ML adoption at scale. The team is the last technical mile between a signed contract and a customer training models in production — and increasingly, the team that decides how fast that happens.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Director, Solutions Architecture, you&#39;ll own the function across [REGION] — the team, the operating model, and the outcomes. You&#39;ll lead managers and senior individual contributors responsible for how W&amp;amp;B is deployed and operated in our largest and most complex accounts, across AWS, GCP, Azure, and on-prem and air-gapped environments. Your central problem is leverage: how technical delivery scales without headcount scaling linearly with revenue, through coverage design, automation, reference architectures, partner enablement, and the management layer you build beneath you. You&#39;ll be a peer to Sales, Field Engineering, Support, and Product leadership — accountable alongside them for adoption, retention, and expansion in region — and you&#39;ll carry the clearest signal we have on customer reality into roadmap and platform investment. Externally, you&#39;ll serve as executive technical sponsor for strategic accounts and the face of W&amp;amp;B engineering credibility in [REGION].&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own Solutions Architecture across [REGION]: strategy, operating model, headcount plan, capacity forecasting, and leveling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and develop the management layer — hire and coach managers and team leads rather than remaining the single escalation point&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define how deployments scale: reference architectures, automation and IaC standards, deployment SLAs, and quality bars across sub-regions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate as a senior cross-functional partner to Sales, Field Engineering, Support, and Product leadership, jointly accountable for regional adoption, retention, and expansion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stand up leverage programs that reduce direct delivery load — customer and partner enablement, certification, self-service tooling, and documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as executive technical sponsor for strategic accounts, including escalation ownership at the CTO and VP Engineering level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate aggregated field evidence into prioritized roadmap and platform investment recommendations with Product and Engineering leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the regional forecast for technical delivery capacity, including partner-led and services-led models where they apply&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years leading a customer-facing technical organization, including 2+ years managing managers or team leads&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years total experience with a hands-on infrastructure, platform, SRE, or solutions engineering foundation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated track record scaling a post-sales or field technical function through a step change in revenue, customer count, or geography — with the coverage, escalation, and SLA model to show for it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical depth sufficient to lead an architecture review: Kubernetes, Helm, containerization, networking, storage, and cloud-managed services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Production experience with Infrastructure as Code, preferably Terraform, and with IaC standards adopted across a team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency across multiple cloud platforms (AWS, GCP, Azure) plus on-prem or self-managed deployment experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Linux/Unix command line experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with ML workflows, MLOps tooling, and how ML platforms are operated in production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience owning a headcount plan and capacity model, including build-versus-partner delivery decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience influencing product roadmap with structured, evidenced field input&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating a distributed team across multiple countries and time zones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep proficiency in Kubernetes design patterns, including Operators and CRDs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building enablement, certification, or partner-delivery programs that measurably reduced direct delivery load&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regulated, sovereign, or air-gapped deployment experience (government, financial services, healthcare, defense)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with GPU infrastructure, large-scale distributed training, and MLOps platform operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a developer-tools or infrastructure company selling to engineering and ML platform teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SaaS, web service, or distributed systems operations experience at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wondering if you&#39;re a good fit?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe in investing in our people, and value candidates who can bring their own diversified experiences to our teams – even if you aren&#39;t a 100% skill or experience match. Here are a few qualities we&#39;ve found compatible with our team. If some of this describes you, we&#39;d love to talk.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You love diving into infrastructure problems and solving them systematically — and you build the teams and systems that keep them solved&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re curious about how to scale complex ML systems in production environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re an expert in building and running containerized, distributed systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You think about leverage first: what automation, documentation, or hire makes the next hundred deployments easier&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable being the technical voice in the room with a customer executive team, and the one who tells Product what they do not want to hear&lt;/li&gt;
