&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Data Center Operations Enablement team helps Data Center Operations work more efficiently and scale effectively by improving workflows, documentation, tools, and operational processes. In this role, you will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Understand and Improve Operational Workflows&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Data Center Operations teams to understand day-to-day workflows, pain points, and operational needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Map existing processes, gather stakeholder feedback, and identify opportunities to improve efficiency and reduce manual work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help standardize processes and improve operational consistency across teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate potential improvements based on operational value, effort, adoption needs, and long-term support requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build and Support Operational Solutions&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and implement internal tools, automations, dashboards, and AI-enabled solutions that address defined operational needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate operational challenges into clear requirements and practical solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Test solutions, gather feedback, resolve common issues, and refine tools based on user needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the deployment, ongoing maintenance, and continuous improvement of operational tools and processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive Adoption and Enablement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and maintain clear documentation, SOPs, user guides, training materials, and support resources.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help employees understand and incorporate new tools and processes into their daily workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gather user feedback and recommend improvements that strengthen adoption and usability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure solutions are documented well enough to be maintained and supported by others.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborate Across Teams&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Operations, Engineering, Infrastructure, Supply Chain, and other partners to deliver operational improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate requirements, progress, risks, and outcomes clearly to both technical and non-technical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong working relationships that support the successful development and adoption of new solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with appropriate partners to move solutions through established review and approval processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Measure and Improve Impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review operational data and metrics to identify trends, recurring challenges, and improvement opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track defined measures such as adoption, time saved, reduced manual effort, fewer errors, and solution health.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use data and stakeholder feedback to recommend practical improvements to tools, processes, and enablement materials.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Enablement Solutions Specialist builds and supports practical tools, processes, and operational improvements that help Data Center Operations work more efficiently and scale effectively. Working closely with operations teams and cross-functional partners, you will identify opportunities to simplify workflows, reduce manual effort, improve documentation, and introduce automation where it adds value.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role combines operational problem-solving, hands-on solution development, documentation, and user enablement. You will work with internal tools, dashboards, AI-enabled solutions, and automation while helping teams adopt new ways of working.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role sits within the Data Center Operations organization and partners closely with Operations, Infrastructure, Engineering, Supply Chain, and business teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to understand operational workflows, identify process gaps, and recommend practical improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience translating operational needs into clear requirements, documented processes, or internal solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience creating and maintaining SOPs, user guides, training materials, or other operational documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to test solutions, gather user feedback, troubleshoot common issues, and iterate on tools or processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with operational metrics and the ability to use data to evaluate adoption, efficiency, errors, or solution health.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage multiple tasks, coordinate follow-up actions, and deliver defined work with guidance when complexity or risk increases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to explain tools and technical concepts to non-technical employees.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in operations, data centers, infrastructure, logistics, manufacturing, or another technical or operational environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with process improvement, workflow management, reporting, automation, or internal tool development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with scripting, SQL, low-code platforms, AI tools, dashboards, or business systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and problem-solving skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wondering if you’re a good fit?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We believe in investing in our people, and value candidates who can bring their own diversified experiences to our teams – even if you aren&#39;t a 100% skill or experience match. Here are a few qualities we’ve found compatible with our team. If some of this describes you, we’d love to talk.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re curious, practical, and motivated to improve how work gets done.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You enjoy understanding operational problems and turning them into useful solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re interested in using technology, automation, and AI to improve workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re comfortable testing your work, gathering feedback, and making improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re organized, detail-oriented, and comfortable working in a fast-paced environment where processes and priorities continue to evolve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re eager to learn new tools and build your technical and operational capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You love to solve complex operational problems and find ways to make workflows more efficient.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re curious about learning how new technologies and automation can improve operational consistency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re an expert in collaborating across diverse teams to translate operational needs into practical, scalable solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why CoreWeave?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At CoreWeave, we work hard, have fun, and move fast! We’re in an exciting stage of hyper-growth that you will not want to miss out on. We’re not afraid of a little chaos, and we’re constantly learning. Our team cares deeply about how we build our product and how we work together, which is represented through our core values:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be Curious at Your Core&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act Like an Owner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Empower Employees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver Best-in-Class Client Experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Achieve More Together&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We support and encourage an entrepreneurial outlook and independent thinking. We foster an environment that encourages collaboration and enables the development of innovative solutions to complex problems. As we get set for takeoff, the organization&#39;s growth opportunities are constantly expanding. You will be surrounded by some of the best talent in the industry, who will want to learn from you, too. Come join us!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base salary range for this role is $99,000 to $145,000. The starting salary will be determined by job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and the market location. We strive for both market alignment and internal equity when determining compensation. In addition to base salary, our total rewards package includes a discretionary bonus, equity awards, and a comprehensive benefits program (all based on eligibility).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The range we’ve posted represents the typical compensation range for this role. To determine actual compensation, we review the market rate for each candidate which can include a variety of factors. These include qualifications, experience, interview performance, and location.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to a competitive salary, we offer a variety of benefits to support your needs. The benefits below reflect our US-based offerings for full-time employees; for roles in other locations, benefits vary and are shared during the hiring process. These include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medical, dental, and vision insurance - 100% paid for by CoreWeave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company-paid Life Insurance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Voluntary supplemental life insurance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Short and long-term disability insurance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible Spending Account&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health Savings Account&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tuition Reimbursement&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to Participate in Employee Stock Purchase Program (ESPP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental Wellness Benefits through Spring Health&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family-Forming support provided by Carrot&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid Parental Leave&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible, full-service childcare support with Kinside&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) with a generous employer match&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible PTO&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Catered lunch each day in our office and data center locations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A casual work environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A work culture focused on innovative disruption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
