&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About The Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CoreWeave is looking for a Field Business Development Manager to own and grow our most strategic partner relationships. This is a high-impact, externally-facing role sitting at the intersection of business development and go-to-market execution. You&#39;ll be the primary point of contact for a portfolio of tier-one partners — including NVIDIA, hyperscalers, and key technology partners — driving joint pipeline, co-sell motions, and mutual customer success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is the partner-side equivalent of a field sales leader: you&#39;ll own relationships, carry influence targets, and be accountable for measurable outcomes. You&#39;ll work closely with CoreWeave&#39;s Sales, Solutions Engineering, and Business Development organizations to align partner initiatives with company priorities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner Relationship Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary field liaison for a portfolio of strategic partners, including NVIDIA, AWS, Google Cloud, Microsoft Azure and select technology ecosystem partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain executive-level relationships at partner organizations, spanning business development and sales stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and manage joint business plans, including co-sell targets, enablement milestones, and GTM initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent CoreWeave at partner QBRs, field events, and executive briefings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Go-to-Market Execution&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive co-sell and influence pipeline in collaboration with CoreWeave&#39;s field sales team and counterpart partner managers at NVIDIA and hyperscalers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, track, and accelerate joint opportunities from sourcing through close, coordinating across both sides of the partnership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop territory-level partner plans aligned to regional sales priorities and quotas&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with partner field teams to ensure CoreWeave is embedded in their customer conversations and solution architectures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner Enablement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead enablement sessions, workshops, and technical briefings to ensure partner sales and technical teams can effectively position and sell CoreWeave solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop joint solution plays and reference architectures in partnership with Solutions Engineering and Product Marketing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a deep understanding of CoreWeave&#39;s product portfolio and competitive differentiation, and translate this into partner-facing messaging and materials&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ecosystem Development&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with the Business Development team to evaluate new partnership opportunities and recommend prioritization based on strategic fit and revenue potential&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to CoreWeave&#39;s partner program development, including tier frameworks, incentives, and co-marketing structures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Measurement &amp;amp; Reporting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and report on partner-influenced and partner-sourced pipeline, revenue, and engagement metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide field-level feedback to the central Business Development and product teams on partner needs, gaps, and competitive dynamics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate records of partner activity and pipeline in Salesforce&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of experience in partner management, alliances, business development, or a related field-facing role at a cloud, infrastructure, or enterprise software company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience managing strategic partnerships with hyperscalers (AWS, Google Cloud, Azure) or major technology ecosystem partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of driving partner-influenced revenue and executing co-sell motions in a field environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong executive presence and ability to build trusted relationships at senior levels inside both CoreWeave and partner organizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional written and verbal communication skills; comfortable presenting to C-suite audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working cross-functionally with sales, marketing, product, and engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly organized and self-directed; able to manage multiple partner relationships and initiatives simultaneously&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience at or with NVIDIA, AWS, Google Cloud, or MSFT Azure in a partner or alliances capacity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in GPU computing, AI/ML infrastructure, Model Ecosystem, MLOps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with cloud co-sell programs (e.g., AWS ACE, Google PSO/ISV programs)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Location&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a field-based role. Candidates must be located in or willing to relocate to one of the following:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;San Francisco, Sunnyvale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;New York&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Travel of approximately 30–40% is expected, including partner site visits, customer meetings, field events, and internal offsites.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;The base salary range for this role is $149,000 to $195,000. The starting salary will be determined based on job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and market location. We strive for both market alignment and internal equity when determining compensation. In addition to base salary, our total rewards package includes a discretionary bonus, equity awards, and a comprehensive benefits program (all based on eligibility).&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The range we’ve posted represents the typical compensation range for this role. To determine actual compensation, we review the market rate for each candidate which can include a variety of factors. These include qualifications, experience, interview performance, and location.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to a competitive salary, we offer a variety of benefits to support your needs. The benefits below reflect our US-based offerings for full-time employees; for roles in other locations, benefits vary and are shared during the hiring process. These include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medical, dental, and vision insurance - 100% paid for by CoreWeave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company-paid Life Insurance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Voluntary supplemental life insurance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Short and long-term disability insurance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible Spending Account&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health Savings Account&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tuition Reimbursement&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to Participate in Employee Stock Purchase Program (ESPP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental Wellness Benefits through Spring Health&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family-Forming support provided by Carrot&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid Parental Leave&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible, full-service childcare support with Kinside&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) with a generous employer match&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible PTO&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Catered lunch each day in our office and data center locations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A casual work environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A work culture focused on innovative disruption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;California Applicants&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gPBRBhUNAMBmj7Yn4_M-hCugm7ZJD4hr/view?usp=sharing&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;California Consumer Privacy Act&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
