&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About CoreWeave&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CoreWeave powers the creation and delivery of the next generation of AI. We provide the infrastructure behind some of the most demanding AI and high-performance computing workloads in the world. As we continue to scale rapidly, finance plays a critical role in helping the business deploy capital thoughtfully, improve efficiency, and translate operational complexity into clear decision-making.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CoreWeave is looking for a Finance Analyst to join the Capacity Finance team within FP&amp;amp;A. This role sits at the intersection of finance, infrastructure, and operations, supporting the planning and analysis behind our global hardware and datacenter footprint.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This person will support forecasting, capacity-related financial modeling, variance analysis, and investment decision support across GPU, CPU, storage, and network infrastructure. They will partner closely with Engineering, Supply Chain, Datacenter Infrastructure, Revenue Finance, Treasury, Accounting, and Corporate FP&amp;amp;A to connect operational plans with financial outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a strong opportunity for someone who enjoys solving complex problems, working with large and changing datasets, and building analyses that directly inform high-impact decisions.&amp;nbsp; Optimally, this person will have previous experience with building large, complex operational models, skills in data organization and automation, exceptional abilities in complex financial modeling and economic analysis, and exemplary written and verbal communication skills.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, maintain, and improve financial models that support capacity planning and infrastructure investment decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support forecast, close, annual planning, and long-range planning processes for Capacity Finance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze actuals versus forecast and explain key variances related to deployment timing, hardware mix, utilization, and cost movements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate operational inputs into financial impacts across CapEx, depreciation, cost of revenue, cash flow, and margin&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Engineering, Supply Chain, Datacenter Infrastructure, and Finance teams to evaluate assumptions, risks, and tradeoffs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and report key capacity and financial KPIs, including metrics tied to utilization, sellable capacity, and capital efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare clear reporting and commentary for Finance leadership and cross-functional stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve reporting consistency, model controls, and planning processes as the business scales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A bachelor’s degree in finance, accounting, applied mathematics, economics, or other business major is required, or an equivalent combination of education and experience&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in FP&amp;amp;A, strategic finance, accounting, consulting, investment banking, or a related analytical role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Excel and modeling skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with large datasets and linking operational drivers to financial outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to structure ambiguous issues into clear outputs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort operating cross-functionally in an environment with changing assumptions and evolving processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High attention to detail and strong sense of ownership in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in datacenter, cloud, hardware, infrastructure, semiconductors, or supply chain finance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Claude, SQL, Tableau, Power Query, or similar tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wondering if you&#39;re a good fit? We believe in investing in our people, and value candidates who can bring their own diversified experiences to our teams – even if you aren&#39;t a 100% skill or experience match. &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why CoreWeave?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot;&gt;At CoreWeave, we work hard, have fun, and move fast! We&#39;re in an exciting stage of hyper-growth that you will not want to miss out on. We&#39;re not afraid of a little chaos, and we&#39;re constantly learning. Our team cares deeply about how we build our product and how we work together, which is represented through our core values:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;[li_&amp;amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be Curious at Your Core&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Act Like an Owner&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Empower Employees&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deliver Best-in-Class Client Experiences&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Achieve More Together&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot;&gt;We support and encourage an entrepreneurial outlook and independent thinking. We foster an environment that encourages collaboration and enables the development of innovative solutions to complex problems. As we get set for takeoff, the organization&#39;s growth opportunities are constantly expanding. You will be surrounded by some of the best talent in the industry, who will want to learn from you, too. Come join us!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;The base salary range for this role is $83,000 to $110,000. The starting salary will be determined based on job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and market location. We strive for both market alignment and internal equity when determining compensation. In addition to base salary, our total rewards package includes a discretionary bonus, equity awards, and a comprehensive benefits program (all based on eligibility).&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
