&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CoreWeave&#39;s Greenfield Accounts organization is responsible for acquiring new customers and expanding CoreWeave&#39;s presence across untapped markets and territories, with aligned Solution Architect coverage supporting technical qualification, deal execution, and customer outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This team sits inside a fast-moving revenue organization and is built to drive new logo growth, open new verticals, and bring new customers onto CoreWeave&#39;s AI-native platform and broader cloud portfolio.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CoreWeave is seeking a Sales Manager for Greenfield Accounts to lead a team of Account Executives focused on new business acquisition within assigned territories.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is responsible for building pipeline, accelerating new logo growth, and leading a high-performing field team in a complex and competitive environment. The right candidate will combine strong frontline sales leadership with operating rigor, cross-functional coordination, and a high bar for new business execution. You will help build a prospecting-first culture, develop opportunity pipelines from the ground up, improve territory coverage, and represent a consolidated view of new business performance to senior leaders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and manage a field sales team focused on greenfield accounts and new customer acquisition.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive new logo growth and pipeline generation across assigned territories.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceed team revenue goals through strong inspection, coaching, and disciplined new business execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scale an integrated go-to-market motion across sales, Solutions Architects, partners, product, and other cross-functional teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and maintain strong relationships with prospective customers while helping the team build executive and working-level engagement from the ground up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run operating cadences across the team, including forecast calls, pipeline inspection, 1:1s, team meetings, and leadership reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clarify territory ownership, manage account coverage, and partner with leadership and RevOps on changes that improve productivity and reduce friction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the talent strategy and outcomes for the team, including hiring, performance management, promotion readiness, and leadership development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support onboarding, product fluency, and consistent new business execution as the team scales.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of technology sales, business development, or related experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of people management experience leading sales teams focused on new business acquisition.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience hiring and leading teams focused on acquiring net new enterprise customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong track record of coaching teams on pipeline generation, prospecting, and new logo revenue performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading teams in cloud, infrastructure, AI platform, or other complex technical sales environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading through cross-functional environments that include technical, partner, and product stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong operating discipline in Salesforce and territory governance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
