&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The CoreWeave Legal and Government Affairs (LGA) team at CoreWeave is highly collaborative and partners closely with teams across the company to navigate complex policy, regulatory, and business environments while enabling innovation and growth. The team is pragmatic, solutions-oriented, and deeply engaged in strategic decision-making, with a strong emphasis on building trusted relationships across the organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Senior Community Affairs &amp;amp; Partnerships Manager, you will lead community engagement across assigned markets and strengthen CoreWeave&#39;s social license to operate. You will build trusted local relationships, guide cross-functional engagement strategies, and ensure community considerations inform site selection, permitting, construction, and operations. If you thrive in a dynamic, fast-paced environment, enjoy solving complex problems, and are eager to make a significant impact, CoreWeave is the place for you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Director, Community Affairs &amp;amp; Partnerships, you will serve as a trusted advisor to senior leadership and will independently assess local risks and opportunities, translate community developments into clear business recommendations, and help ensure the company makes informed decisions throughout the project lifecycle.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will lead the development and negotiation of community benefit agreements and support PILOTs, RDAs, and other development agreements that advance CoreWeave&#39;s business objectives while creating meaningful value for host communities. You will also oversee local partnerships and community investments and work with CoreWeave Cares and our Employee Action Networks to direct employee-driven community impact toward the markets where CoreWeave operates.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role you will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and lead cross-functional community engagement strategies across assigned markets, partnering with Government Affairs, Communications, People, Legal, Development, Operations, and other teams to align engagement with business objectives, permitting milestones, construction schedules, and operational priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead Community Affairs input into site selection and project due diligence, assessing community sentiment, political dynamics, stakeholder priorities, local opposition, and reputational risk in prospective and active markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain trusted relationships with elected officials, community leaders, faith-based organizations, nonprofits, unions, business groups, and other local stakeholders; represent CoreWeave in community, political, and public forums.&lt;/li&gt;
