&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Firmware Engineer, you will drive the development and evolution of our UEFI/BIOS ecosystem and influence future server architecture decisions. Leveraging deep expertise in x86 and ARM64 architectures, you will architect secure, scalable firmware solutions tailored for CoreWeave&#39;s high-performance AI infrastructure. You will own complex technical challenges, lead cross-functional initiatives with hardware and security teams, and partner with key silicon vendors to optimize our custom server stack for next-generation compute capabilities. You will architect and refine mission-critical systems on state-of-the-art server platforms and next-generation silicon, exercising end-to-end ownership of core firmware components from conceptual design through global deployment, while collaborating with industry-leading innovators to define the future of high-performance cloud computing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect and implement advanced UEFI/BIOS features optimized for large-scale server deployments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diagnose and resolve intricate firmware vulnerabilities and bugs using ITP, JTAG, and hardware debuggers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Streamline platform initialization and boot sequences to enhance system responsiveness and efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate robust secure boot protocols and hardware-root-of-trust mechanisms to safeguard firmware integrity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engineer and maintain critical Power-On Self Test (POST) logic for diverse hardware configurations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design seamless remote firmware update and recovery pipelines for fleet-wide reliability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead technical collaboration on board bring-up, hardware validation, and platform stabilization efforts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;UEFI/BIOS Development&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain high-performance UEFI/BIOS codebases for server ecosystems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement ACPI tables and power management logic to optimize system efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Debug critical bottlenecks using ITP and JTAG methodologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage ODM partnerships and BIOS development lifecycles, ensuring alignment on firmware specifications, quality, and delivery milestones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with silicon vendors (Intel, AMD, Nvidia) to orchestrate the integration and rebasing of Reference Code packages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Align firmware capabilities with product management objectives and market needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide technical leadership for firmware features and mentor junior talent to foster a high-performing engineering culture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead strategic technical planning for roadmaps while reviewing architectural specs and enforcing rigorous coding standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
