&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CoreWeave is expanding its firmware engineering organization to support next-generation AI compute platforms and the integrated firmware stack that powers them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Firmware Engineer, FPGA &amp;amp; Platform Integration, you will design, implement, validate, and maintain FPGA-based platform functionality while ensuring clean integration with BMC firmware, BIOS, and hardware platforms deployed across CoreWeave’s data centers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work independently on complex technical problems, partner closely with hardware, firmware, and systems teams, and help define best practices for platform reliability, observability, and maintainability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Some of what you’ll work on:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;FPGA development – design, implement, and maintain FPGA logic for server-class or embedded platform functions, with a strong emphasis on Intel/Altera-based devices using Quartus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Platform integration – define and implement interfaces between FPGA logic and adjacent platform components including BMC firmware, BIOS, CPLDs, sensors, control paths, and board management functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring-up and validation – support early hardware enablement, board bring-up, and validation across multiple hardware revisions and lab environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-layer debugging – diagnose complex issues spanning FPGA logic, firmware, BIOS, hardware interfaces, and operating systems using appropriate lab and debug tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performance and reliability – improve platform robustness, fault handling, telemetry, and operational behavior for production deployments at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Vendor collaboration – work directly with ODMs, silicon vendors, and firmware partners to review implementations, define requirements, and drive fixes or enhancements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automation and test – contribute to repeatable validation workflows, regression coverage, and tooling for FPGA and platform firmware testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Documentation – create and maintain clear technical documentation for FPGA architecture, interfaces, design assumptions, test procedures, and operational considerations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical leadership – participate in design reviews, mentor other engineers, and help raise the overall quality of firmware and platform integration work across the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of professional experience in firmware, embedded systems, or FPGA development for server-class, platform, or embedded systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Computer Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Computer Science, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on professional experience developing with Intel/Altera FPGA devices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong proficiency in Verilog or SystemVerilog for RTL development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong proficiency in C or C++ for low-level firmware, embedded software, or platform integration work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with board bring-up, hardware validation, and system-level debugging.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with common hardware interfaces and protocols such as I2C, SPI, UART, GPIO, PCIe, or related platform control paths.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in using hardware schematics, design specifications, and device datasheets for embedded development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience debugging interactions across FPGA, firmware, BIOS, and hardware layers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working in Linux environments with Git-based development workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and problem-solving skills with the ability to break down complex cross-layer failures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills and the ability to collaborate effectively across hardware, firmware, software, QA, and vendor teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience integrating FPGA functionality with BMC firmware, BIOS, CPLDs, or other platform management components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with LTPI or similar platform communication and management interfaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with platform management technologies such as Redfish, IPMI, SMBus, or related server management interfaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with server hardware, data center platforms, or hyperscale infrastructure environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with lab tools and techniques such as logic analyzers, oscilloscopes, JTAG, signal capture, or board-level debug workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience scripting in Python or Bash for validation, automation, or test tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience reviewing or influencing vendor-delivered platform or firmware implementations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior ownership of firmware or FPGA features deployed into production environments at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why CoreWeave?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At CoreWeave, you’ll work on the platform foundation behind some of the world’s most advanced AI infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role sits at a highly technical intersection of FPGA development, platform firmware integration, and large-scale operational reliability. You’ll help shape how critical platform functions are implemented, validated, and operated across next-generation compute systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;The base salary range for this role is $182,000 to $242,000. The starting salary will be determined based on job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and market location. We strive for both market alignment and internal equity when determining compensation. In addition to base salary, our total rewards package includes a discretionary bonus, equity awards, and a comprehensive benefits program (all based on eligibility).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The range we’ve posted represents the typical compensation range for this role. To determine actual compensation, we review the market rate for each candidate which can include a variety of factors. These include qualifications, experience, interview performance, and location.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to a competitive salary, we offer a variety of benefits to support your needs. The benefits below reflect our US-based offerings for full-time employees; for roles in other locations, benefits vary and are shared during the hiring process. These include:&lt;/p&gt;
