&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The AI Dev Platform Tooling team builds and operates the SaaS platform that lets our engineers ship software quickly, reliably, and safely. We own the deployment automation, infrastructure provisioning and monitoring, and release systems — built on a Go, Kubernetes, Terraform, and PostgreSQL stack — that underpin our engineering organization’s ability to deliver software to customers across GCP, AWS, Azure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a Senior Software Engineer to design, build, and operate the backend services and APIs at the core of our SaaS infrastructure. This is primarily a backend software engineering role: you’ll write Go running on Kubernetes, manage state in PostgreSQL, and provision infrastructure with Terraform across multiple public clouds. You’ll evolve designs to meet increasingly challenging scale, stability, and performance demands, and own large, ambiguous problems end to end. We care deeply about a sustainable on-call culture, so you’ll participate in on-call rotations while championing the architecture that reduces on-call burden over time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, deploy, and operate critical backend services and APIs that power our SaaS infrastructure across AWS, GCP, Azure, and customer-managed environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Treat API design as a first-class concern, defining clean, durable interfaces that internal and external consumers depend on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evolve system designs to meet increasingly challenging scale, stability, and performance requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Break down and solve large, ambiguous problems, turning them into well-scoped, shippable engineering work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reduce on-call burden through better architecture, automation, and observability — and participate in on-call rotations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide technical leadership and mentorship, work alongside Principal Engineers, and influence the broader technical direction of the platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to frontend web clients where it accelerates the team (a plus, not a requirement).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of professional software engineering experience designing, building, deploying, and operating critical backend services across a large enterprise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep, hands-on expertise with our core stack: Go, Kubernetes, Terraform, and PostgreSQL.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience with one or more major public clouds (AWS, GCP, or Azure).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong API design skills, with a track record of building interfaces that scale and last.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to evolve designs to meet increasingly challenging scale, stability, and performance requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to break down and solve large, ambiguous problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable owning on-call for services you build, and passionate about reducing on-call burden through architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to provide technical leadership to team members, work effectively with Principal Engineers, influence technical direction, and contribute to the success of cross-functional stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and operating SaaS products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with CI/CD systems (GitHub Actions, Jenkins, etc.) and monitoring/observability tooling (Prometheus, Datadog, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wondering if you’re a good fit?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;We believe in investing in our people, and value candidates who can bring their own diversified experiences to our teams – even if you aren&#39;t a 100% skill or experience match. Here are a few qualities we’ve found compatible with our team. If some of this describes you, we’d love to talk.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You love designing and operating backend services that scale gracefully under pressure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re curious about reducing on-call burden through better architecture rather than more heroics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re an expert in building critical services on a Go, Kubernetes, Terraform, and PostgreSQL stack.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Why CoreWeave?&lt;br&gt;At CoreWeave, we work hard, have fun, and move fast! We’re in an exciting stage of hyper-growth that you will not want to miss out on. We’re not afraid of a little chaos, and we’re constantly learning. Our team cares deeply about how we build our product and how we work together, which is represented through our core values:&lt;/p&gt;
