&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Technical Project Management team at CoreWeave is the operational engine supporting the global build-out and fit-out of our physical infrastructure. As our site footprint expands exponentially, this team manages the critical transition from capacity planning to live operations. TPMs are responsible for managing multiple large-scale projects with aggressive timelines, ensuring that every data center is delivered on time, within scope, and ready for high-performance AI workloads.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Technical Project Manager, you will manage the execution of massive infrastructure projects, taking sites from signing through to day 2 operations. You will lead the delivery and installation of critical hardware, cabling, and network systems, working in a fast-paced environment where timelines are often fluid and expedited. Your mission is to ensure that project blockers are removed and that infrastructure is deployed to CoreWeave&#39;s exacting standards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this role, you will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Project Planning and Execution: Lead the full lifecycle of multiple simultaneous data center deployment projects, including design, construction, testing, commissioning, and handover to operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stakeholder Management: Act as the primary point of contact for stakeholders, including clients, vendors, contractors, and internal teams. Facilitate clear communication and collaboration across all parties involved and hold meetings with your vendors and site to meet timelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resource Management: Effectively manage and allocate resources (teams, tools, budget), ensuring that all project phases are adequately staffed and equipped to meet fast-paced timelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Risk Management: Identify potential project risks, create mitigation strategies, and proactively address issues to minimize disruptions to project timelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scheduling &amp;amp; Budgeting: Develop and maintain project schedules, budgets, and resource plans, ensuring projects are delivered within agreed contractual constraints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quality Assurance: Ensure that all data center deployments meet technical and quality standards, including compliance with industry best practices and local regulations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Documentation: Maintain comprehensive project documentation, including design documents, and give regular progress reports.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical Oversight and Collaboration: Provide technical guidance to teams, in collaboration with experts, on best practices for data center design and deployment, including considerations for power, cooling, networking, and physical security.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continual Improvement: Identify opportunities to optimize processes and improve operational efficiency. Implement best practices and innovative solutions to enhance data center operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Project Oversight: Travel to up to 60% of data center locations to monitor progress, troubleshoot issues, and ensure smooth project execution. Coordinate with local teams, contractors, and vendors during on-site visits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of demonstrated experience in data center deployment, infrastructure project implementation, or technical project management within a data center environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Project Management Skills: Proven ability to successfully manage complex technical projects from initiation to completion, utilizing a strong understanding of project management methodologies and tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data Center Operations: In-depth technical knowledge of data center infrastructure, including servers, storage, networking, power, and cooling systems. Demonstrated familiarity with data center best practices and industry standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leadership and Communication: Demonstrated ability to lead and manage teams, coupled with strong communication and interpersonal skills for effective collaboration with cross-functional teams and stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Problem Solving: Exceptional ability to analyze complex technical issues, troubleshoot problems, and propose innovative solutions, supported by strong decision-making and critical-thinking abilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compliance and Security: Familiarity with industry standards (e.g., TIA-942, Uptime Institute, ASHRAE), data center compliance requirements, security protocols, and risk management practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexibility and Adaptability: Proven ability to prioritize tasks, adapt to changing requirements, and perform effectively in a fast-paced, dynamic environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness and ability to travel up to 60% to data center locations to support project execution, sometimes on short notice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Education: A Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, or a related technical field, or equivalent practical experience. Relevant professional certifications (e.g., PMP, PRINCE2, ITIL, CDCP, CDCS, or similar) are a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with High-Performance Computing (HPC) or AI-specific infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with liquid-to-chip cooling technologies and advanced data center redundancy protocols.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wondering if you’re a good fit?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We believe in investing in our people, and value candidates who can bring their own diversified experiences to our teams – even if you aren&#39;t a 100% skill or experience match. Here are a few qualities we’ve found compatible with our team. If some of this describes you, we’d love to talk.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You love to manage the full lifecycle of complex technical projects in high-growth environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re curious about the future of computing and interested in learning about HPC and AI infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re an expert at navigating ambiguity and thriving in a startup culture where &quot;chaos&quot; is turned into order.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable with significant travel, averaging 3 days per week to various project sites.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why CoreWeave?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At CoreWeave, we work hard, have fun, and move fast! We’re in an exciting stage of hyper-growth that you will not want to miss out on. We’re not afraid of a little chaos, and we’re constantly learning. Our team cares deeply about how we build our product and how we work together, which is represented through our core values:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be Curious at Your Core&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Act Like an Owner&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Empower Employees&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deliver Best-in-Class Client Experiences&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Achieve More Together&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We support and encourage an entrepreneurial outlook and independent thinking. We foster an environment that encourages collaboration and enables the development of innovative solutions to complex problems. As we get set for takeoff, the organization&#39;s growth opportunities are constantly expanding. You will be surrounded by some of the best talent in the industry, who will want to learn from you, too. Come join us!&lt;/p&gt;
