&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a highly skilled Staff Business Systems Engineer – Tax Technology to lead the strategy, architecture, implementation, and optimization of our global tax technology landscape. This role will serve as the technical leader for tax platforms, partnering closely with Tax, Finance, Accounting, IT Engineering, and business stakeholders to deliver scalable, compliant, and automated tax solutions that support CoreWeave&#39;s rapid global growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate brings deep expertise in multiple tax engines (Vertex, Avalara, 1Source etc.),&amp;nbsp; with strong indirect tax domain knowledge, and hands-on experience integrating tax platforms with ERP, billing, procurement, and enterprise applications. This individual will drive the modernization of tax technology while ensuring compliance, operational efficiency, and enterprise scalability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the architecture, implementation, enhancement, and support of tax solutions across global operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design scalable tax technology solutions supporting Sales &amp;amp; Use Tax, VAT, GST, excise tax, withholding tax, and other indirect tax requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Global Tax, Finance, Accounting, Revenue, Procurement, and Engineering teams to define and implement tax system strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, implement, and maintain integrations between tax platforms and enterprise applications including NetSuite, SAP, Workday, Salesforce, Coupa, billing platforms, e-commerce platforms, procurement systems, and data warehouses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support global tax determination, tax calculation, exemption certificate management, tax reporting, tax returns, and audit requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead tax technology projects from requirements gathering through architecture, development, testing, deployment, and post-production support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive automation of tax processes to improve accuracy, compliance, operational efficiency, and scalability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure tax systems comply with SOX controls, audit requirements, data governance policies, and regulatory standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with business stakeholders to evaluate new tax regulations and implement required system changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop technical designs, integration specifications, and solution documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot complex tax calculation, integration, and compliance issues across enterprise applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish best practices for tax technology architecture, integrations, monitoring, and operational support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary technical subject matter expert for tax platforms and enterprise tax systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
